From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xinyang <xinyang@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: quiesce the IRQ thread before taking core->lock (7.3.4)

iris_core_deinit() takes core->lock while the IRQ thread may already hold
it. iris_vpu_power_off() then calls disable_irq() from inside that lock,
and disable_irq() waits for the IRQ thread to finish, so a thread that is
blocked on core->lock deadlocks the unload.

Disable the IRQ before taking the lock and re-enable it after releasing
it, balanced independently of the power state.

Adapted from Project SunUEFI's 0004-media.patch (GPL-2.0-only).
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
index 8c335db..6a72885 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
@@ -16,6 +16,11 @@ void iris_core_deinit(struct iris_core *core)

 	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(core->dev);

+	/* The IRQ thread takes core->lock. Quiesce it before taking that lock,
+	 * otherwise power_off's disable_irq() can wait for a thread blocked on
+	 * us. Keep this extra disable balanced independently of power state.
+	 */
+	disable_irq(core->irq);
 	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
 	if (core->state != IRIS_CORE_DEINIT) {
 		iris_fw_unload(core);
@@ -27,6 +32,7 @@ void iris_core_deinit(struct iris_core *core)
 		core->state = IRIS_CORE_DEINIT;
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&core->lock);
+	enable_irq(core->irq);

 	if (!ret)
 		pm_runtime_put_sync(core->dev);
--
